# Shared helpers and evidence catalogues are supplied by build.py.
content=head('Cohen &amp; Katz / London, Sydney &amp; Johannesburg','Across oceans.<br>Through generations.','Lewis and Rebecca, their children Isaac, David and Dolly, and the family lives that followed in South Africa, Canada and Israel.')
content+='<div class="branch-toolbar"><a href="#household">The London household</a><a href="#journey">Sydney &amp; quarantine</a><a href="#david">David &amp; Millie</a><a href="#leonard">Leonard</a><a href="#freed">The Freed connection</a><a href="#questions">Open questions</a></div>'
content+='<div class="gallery">'+img('cohen-lewis.jpg','Portrait of Lewis Cohen','Lewis, David’s father. Identified by Mark; date unknown.','cohen-lewis-photo')+img('cohen-rebecca.jpg','Portrait of Rebecca Katz Cohen','Rebecca, David’s mother. Identified by Mark; date unknown.','cohen-rebecca-photo')+'</div>'
content+='<div class="reading-width prose">'
content+=section('Lewis and Rebecca: the starting household',p('Mark’s paternal line runs from <a href="people.html#lewis-cohen">Lewis Cohen</a> and <a href="people.html#rebecca-katz">Rebecca Katz</a>, through their son <a href="people.html#david-cohen">David</a> and grandson <a href="people.html#leonard-cohen">Leonard Lewis Cohen</a>, to Mark. The family account names three children of Lewis and Rebecca: <strong>Isaac (Harry), David and Deby (Dolly)</strong>.','cohen-mark')+p('The supplied tree gives Lewis’s birth around 1879, Rebecca’s around 1878 in Poland, their marriage in 1899, and Rebecca’s father as Yitzchak. It places the household in Mile End Old Town at the 1911 census. These details are retained as family-tree information; the census, marriage and birth originals have not yet been inspected.','cohen-mark')+p('Rebecca’s reported death is <strong>4 July 1953</strong>, and Lewis’s <strong>1 May 1963</strong>, both in Johannesburg. Their original death and estate records remain research targets.','cohen-mark'),id='household')
content+=section('The family chart','<p>Relationships below come from Mark’s family account. Follow each name to its evidence notes. The chart does not supply missing dates.</p>'+cite('cohen-mark')+'<div class="gil-family"><div class="gil-parents"><a href="people.html#lewis-cohen"><strong>Lewis Cohen</strong><span>c.1879–1963, family tree</span></a><a href="people.html#rebecca-katz"><strong>Rebecca Katz</strong><span>c.1878–1953, family tree</span></a></div><div class="gil-siblings"><a href="people.html#harry-cohen"><strong>Isaac / Harry</strong><span>Later life unresolved</span></a><a href="people.html#david-cohen"><strong>David + Millie Kavin</strong><span>Parents of Leonard Lewis</span></a><a href="people.html#dolly-cohen"><strong>Dolly / Deby</strong><span>Lucille’s mother in family account</span></a></div></div><p><a href="tree.html">Open the interactive branch diagrams</a>.</p>')
content+=section('London to Sydney, 1913',p('The <strong>Rangatira</strong> outbound list is dated <strong>6 February 1913</strong>, London. The ship was bound for New Zealand, but the Cohen family was booked to land at <strong>Sydney</strong>, with New South Wales as the intended future residence. Lewis is described as a farm hand; all five travelled third class under ticket H56.','cohen-outward')+img('cohen-manifest-1913.jpg','Rangatira outbound passenger list with the five Cohen entries','The Cohen household appears midway down the page. Open the scan to inspect ages, landing port and occupation.','cohen-outward')+p('The NSW arrival transcription lists the same family at Sydney on <strong>20 March 1913</strong>. Mark confirms the identification and remembers that they lived in <strong>Bondi</strong> for a time. Their Bondi address, length of stay and subsequent voyage to South Africa remain unknown.','cohen-sydney','cohen-mark')+'<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Ages that still need resolving</caption><thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>1913 manifest</th><th>Supplied family tree</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Lewis / Mrs Cohen</td><td>33 / 33</td><td>Born c.1879 / c.1878</td></tr><tr><td>Isaac</td><td>11</td><td>Born 1900</td></tr><tr><td>Davey / David</td><td>8</td><td>Born 8 January 1903; would be 10</td></tr><tr><td>Debra / Dolly</td><td>5</td><td>Born c.1906</td></tr></tbody></table></div>'+cite('cohen-outward','cohen-mark')+p('The discrepancies stay visible. They are not grounds to invent corrected birth dates or an explanation for the recorded ages.','cohen-mark'),id='journey')
content+=section('Quarantine and the ship’s later fate',p('Mark remembers a quarantine episode on arrival, and accepts <strong>measles</strong> as the corrected illness. Harbour Trust notes describe a 21-month-old Rangatira passenger who died of measles at North Head Quarantine Station on <strong>23 March 1913</strong>. This supports the ship’s quarantine connection; it does not establish that any Cohen was ill or admitted.','cohen-mark','cohen-quarantine')+p('Sydney’s later 1913 smallpox epidemic is traced by the National Museum to <strong>Zealandia</strong>, arriving on 12 April. It should not be merged with the Rangatira episode.','cohen-smallpox')+p('Rangatira was subsequently wrecked near <strong>Robben Island in March 1916</strong>, three years after this journey. The archaeological survey lists 31 March; a later press account gives 30 March. The family was not identified as aboard at the wreck.','cohen-wreck'))
content+=section('David, Millie and Keens',p('Mark remembers David as a successful businessman, owner of <strong>Keens, an electrical wholesaler</strong>. A 1945 official notice provides a concrete business record: David Cohen and Alec Natas had operated Keens at <strong>22 Montreal House, 118 President Street, Johannesburg</strong>. Following Natas’s retirement, David continued for his own account and benefit. The notice is dated <strong>20 April 1945</strong>.','cohen-mark','cohen-keens')+p('Mark recalls a later Keens office at <strong>246 Main Street</strong>, and a corner involving Main and Marshall streets in Jeppe. The exact address and chronology have not been verified. He also recalls David selling Keens. Bidvest’s 2007 directory lists Keens Electrical within Voltex, but the intervening sale and ownership chain remain unproved.','cohen-mark','cohen-voltex')+p('David and <a href="people.html#millie-kavin">Millie Kavin</a> were Leonard’s parents. No marriage certificate has yet been inspected.','cohen-mark'),id='david')
content+=section('40 Central Street, Houghton',p('Mark remembers David’s home as a <strong>two-acre property at 40 Central Street</strong>, alongside a substantial property and equities portfolio, including land on the Vaal River. The scale and portfolio are family recollection, awaiting estate and title records.','cohen-mark')+p('The property trail is unusually specific: in <strong>1989, Millie Cohen applied concerning erven 1752 and 1753, Houghton Estate</strong>; a 1991 notice records approval under scheme 2539 and cites deed T7788/54. A <strong>1997 notice explicitly places erf 1752 at 40 Central Street, Lower Houghton</strong>. This strongly connects the earlier Millie notice to the remembered family home, but does not establish acreage or ownership succession.','cohen-houghton-1989','cohen-houghton-1991','cohen-houghton-1997')+p('David’s gravestone confirms <strong>16 July 1980</strong>. Mark supplies grave <strong>TT 1166</strong>. The Hebrew appears to name him as <strong>David son of Leib</strong>; that reading remains provisional. The English memorial remembers his wife, children, grandchildren and sister. Its plural wording is not an independent count of biological children.','cohen-david-stone','cohen-mark')+img('cohen-david-stone.png','David Cohen gravestone','David Cohen, died 16 July 1980. Photograph supplied by Mark.','cohen-david-stone'))
content+=section('A collection remembered',p('Mark recalls David owning a large collection of Africana. While away and unsure he would return to South Africa, David reportedly instructed <strong>his mother Rebecca</strong> to donate it to Wits University. The date, contents and completion of the donation are unverified. Verification has been deferred at Mark’s request.','cohen-mark'))
content+=section('Isaac (Harry) and Dolly',img('cohen-harry.png','Isaac Harry Cohen as a child','Isaac (Harry), identified by Mark. Date and location unknown.','cohen-harry-photo')+p('Isaac’s later life remains largely undocumented here. Dolly appears as Deby in the supplied tree and probably Debra in the family’s 1913 entry. Her later surname, spouse and death date are not established. Mark identifies Lucille as her daughter; her earlier surname has not been established.','cohen-mark','cohen-outward'))
content+=section('Leonard Lewis Cohen',p('Leonard, Mark’s father, was born on <strong>2 June 1941</strong>. The supplied Capetown Castle arrival list records him at Southampton on <strong>24 December 1959</strong>, a single South African student planning a ten-day visit. This is a later visit, separate from the 1913 household migration.','cohen-leonard-arrival','cohen-mark')+img('cohen-leonard-arrival.jpg','Capetown Castle passenger list with Leonard Lewis Cohen','Leonard’s entry is near the foot of the page, row 234.','cohen-leonard-arrival')+p('His gravestone records death on <strong>30 January 1995</strong>, and the Hebrew name <strong>Yehuda Leib son of David ha-Kohen</strong>. Plot U7422 is visible.','cohen-leonard-stone')+img('cohen-leonard-stone.jpeg','Leonard Lewis Cohen gravestone','Leonard Lewis Cohen, 1941–1995; birth date from the arrival list, death date from the stone.','cohen-leonard-stone'),id='leonard')
content+=section('Lucille, Brian and the Freed connection',p('Mark identifies <a href="people.html#lucille-freed">Lucille</a> as Dolly’s daughter and <a href="people.html#brian-freed">Brian Freed</a> as her husband. He remembers their move to Toronto and children Nadine, Darryl, Kim and an older sister whose name he could not recall.','cohen-mark')+p('Public comments dated <strong>16 July 2017</strong>, attributed to Brian and Lucille Freed, name <strong>Lauren, Daryl, Nadine and Kim</strong> in descending age order. This is a strong match to the household Mark describes: Lauren is likely the unnamed older sister, and the source spells Daryl with one r. The comments do not themselves establish the Dolly relationship.','cohen-freed-comments')+p('The couple wrote that they had spent forty years in Canada and six in Israel. Approximate moves around 1971 and 2011 are inferences, not exact migration dates. Their present residence is not established. Brian also names Jonathan as his younger brother and Justin as Jonathan’s son; those collateral links remain attributed to the comment rather than independently documented.','cohen-freed-comments')+'<p>Living descendants are represented with names and essential family links only; contact details and detailed personal profiles are not reproduced.</p>',id='freed')
content+=section('What remains to be found','<ul><li>Lewis and Rebecca’s marriage, exact birthplaces and parents.</li><li>The original 1911 census household, to resolve the children’s ages.</li><li>The Bondi address and Australia–South Africa passage.</li><li>David’s estate file, using death 16 July 1980, wife Millie, Keens and 40 Central Street as identifiers.</li><li>Keens’ sale date and buyer; the Vaal property titles and estate inventory.</li><li>Harry’s later life and Dolly’s married surname and dates.</li></ul><p>No estate file or portfolio valuation has yet been obtained. A name-only match is not treated as a completed family identification.</p>',id='questions')
content+='</div>'
page('cohen.html','The Cohen and Katz family',content)
